==English==

===Etymology===
Compound of {{compound|red|neck}} (referring to the red neckerchiefs worn by unionized workers during the mine wars in West Virginia) Unionized works wearing red (Communist) neckerchiefs could easily seen from a distance.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}


# {{slang}} The nickname given to miners who wore red [[bandana]]s for identification during the West Virginia mine war of 1921.  <ref>[http://www.wvculture.org/hiStory/minewars.html West Virginia Division of Culture and History]</ref>

====Synonyms====
* [[cracker]]
* [[peckerwood]]
* [[white trash]]

